# Normalize line endings to LF in the repo AND on checkout. Two reasons that are specific
# rather than tidiness:
#
# 1. `.githooks/*` are `#!/bin/sh` scripts git executes directly. With core.autocrlf=true
#    a checkout would hand them CRLF line endings, and a shell that carries the CR into
#    the interpreter path or a line continuation fails in a way that reads as "the hook
#    is broken" rather than "the checkout rewrote it".
# 2. CI runs on Windows and on Linux, and a line-ending class of failure is invisible to
#    a Linux-only leg: identical counts, diverging digests. A repo whose content hashes
#    depend on which platform checked it out cannot be compared across the two.
* text=auto eol=lf
